TODO list (incomplete)

This is a Bestechnic BES2600 / BEST2002 SDIO mac80211 driver (CW1200-family
WSM firmware protocol).  On PineTab2 v2.0 (RK3566, mmc2) STA Wi-Fi works on
branch wifi-good (058ba083bc1e and later): firmware load, idle scan, open and
WPA2 associate, 4-way, DHCP, ping, FAST_PS on APs that implement it, associated
scan after FAST_PS is proven, and switching between APs.  Bluetooth has never
worked.

The driver was previously removed from staging for quality.  Do not send it
upstream until timeouts and RF misses cannot oops the machine, and the
vendor/debug leftovers below are gone.  BUG_ON and WARN_ON are already
gone from live paths.

Test a FAST_PS-ok BSS and a PS-bad BSS (if you have both), both directions,
after every change.  First association after boot is not enough.  Gate:
ping -4 both ways.  No per-SSID hacks.

Firmware is still Dec 2023 (best2002_fw_boot_sdio.bin / best2002_fw_sdio.bin,
8125e20be).  No newer public SDIO LMAC blob.

Proven working (STA, PineTab2 v2.0, firmware Dec 2023, wifi-good)
-------------------------------------------------------------------
* Probe, boot + main firmware, phy registration.
* STA + P2P_DEVICE vifs (P2P is host-only; see below).
* Idle scan: 2.4 GHz then 5 GHz, firmware scan-complete status 0.
* Open and WPA2-CCMP association, 4-way, DHCP, ping.
* Switching BSS after a working session, including 4-way after an open
  BSS.  Occasional first WPA2 4-way still loses M3 (below).
* Do not force_close the SDIO bus on -EBUSY (hard-locks the SoC).
* No live BUG_ON or WARN_ON.  Firmware NAK / SDIO timeout / no-ACK log with
  bes_err / bes_fail and keep the errno; they must not taint.
* Firmware load logs on the SDIO function (global_dev set in sdio_probe;
  macros fall back to pr_* if it is still NULL).

Do not regress those without a replacement that has been tested on hardware.

Power save / associated scan (current contract)
----------------------------------------------
This LMAC's power save is firmware-owned and poorly documented.  FAST_PS
(0x81) is the only mode that actually enters PS (0x0809 psm=0x1).  Legacy
0x01 never does.  Whether a given AP's FAST_PS is usable is also outside
the host: some APs keep unicast IP working, some do not.  Host work is
detect and work around, not "make the AP or the blob do IEEE PS correctly".
A better PS mode may exist; it would need LMAC documentation we do not have.

SUPPORTS_PS + SUPPORTS_DYNAMIC_PS; cfg.ps=1 → 0x81 even when dyn_to=0
(this stack means "firmware owns idle").  Cache then send 0x0010; do not
wait for 0x0809.  Do not wsm_set_pm from BH/RX or from bes_pwr MCU
sleep/wake (0x0010 is owned by sta.c).  Skip MCU sleep while the firmware
is in 802.11 PS (quiescent 0x0006 hung this LMAC).

Two classes of BSS:
* FAST_PS-ok: 0x0809 psm=0x1, unicast IP continues, associated scan
  status=0.
* PS-bad: either the firmware never enters psm=0x1, or it does and
  unicast IP dies.  Stay ACTIVE, no associated scan.

Once per association:
* Pass: unicast IP RX after FAST_PS settled (~1s).  "FAST_PS ok, stop probe".
* Fail: ICMP echo or TCP SYN with 802.11 ACK and no IP RX for 8s → ap_ps_bad,
  stay ACTIVE, no associated scan.
* ARP/DHCP/DNS/TCP payload are not probes (false-failed FAST_PS-ok APs).
* 0x0809 psm=0 (fw stayed ACTIVE): retry FAST_PS up to 3 times, then PS-bad.
  One refuse after roam is not a verdict.
* Do not enter FAST_PS / do not fail the probe if RETRY_EXCEEDED after the
  last IP RX (flaky 5 GHz).

Associated scan: BACKGROUND + FORCE_BACKGROUND, 10/25 TU, one channel per
0x0007, TX locked for the whole request.  Never foreground 0x0007 while
joined, never wsm_reset() on scan failure while STA.  -EBUSY until FAST_PS
is proven (ap_ps_checked && !ap_ps_bad).  PS-bad APs stay unanswered/ACTIVE
and scans busy by design.  On associated scan timeout, send 0x0008 stop-scan
(skipping it left LMAC off-channel and DNS died).  wsm_oper_lock times out
at 10s.  scan_work drops conf_lock before 0x0007 (prevents deauth/rtnl hang).

After associated scan the driver may still wsm_switch_channel (narrow to
HT20 on the way in, restore type/home on the way out).  BACKGROUND scan
is supposed to return to the home channel itself.  Double-check whether
that extra channel-setting switch is still needed; it may be leftover
from foreground/idle scan.

Host ADDBA is dropped; firmware owns ADDBA.  BA after PS is settled, not
after an EAPOL ACK.  Unjoin sends BA policy 0.  Join-after-unjoin: wsm_reset
drops FW frames with no confirm; host zeros hw_bufs_used.

Do not send 0x0010 ACTIVE from leave-BSS just to be tidy when already
ACTIVE (unjoin wsm_reset is enough).  ACTIVE+AMPDU in firmware caused a 6s
confirm timeout → SDIO -16.  Leaving a FAST_PS BSS may still send ACTIVE;
that path has completed quickly in recent logs.

Mainline still wants associated scan on every BSS.  This LMAC cannot do it
while stuck ACTIVE on a PS-bad AP.  Keep the probe; do not special-case
SSIDs.

WARN_ON / BUG_ON
----------------
Done on live paths (003b791664bb BUG_ON, a9925f9a0ee6 WARN_ON).  Remaining
mentions are comments.  Do not put WARN_ON back on firmware NAK, SDIO
timeout, or "AP did not ACK".  147ad3eaca60 converted those blindly and
broke reconnect; the later conversion kept the same if/return and only
removed taint.

Broken commits (wifi-broken, do not replay as a lump)
-----------------------------------------------------
* 0d7099dbf846 rate-limit / weak-signal: WPA2 BSS still worked, open BSS
  always failed.  The 1 Mbps clamp and related TX policy belong here.
* 26ee084ec255 same open-fail / WPA2-ok pattern.
* c426582bf6ff associated-scan: BACKGROUND + FORCE_BACKGROUND, no
  wsm_reset while STA.  Bare BACKGROUND of NM's 14+27 channels at 100 ms
  dwell while staying ACTIVE killed AMPDU.  Do not toggle BA 0/177 around
  scan.  Do not skip associated scan with a blanket -EBUSY; the current
  gate is FAST_PS proven, not "associated ⇒ busy".
* d6c2ab442ff4 mainline-prep: broken.
* 147ad3eaca60 WARN_ON/BUG_ON: first connect after boot worked; later
  connects failed.  Do not re-apply that conversion blindly.

Logging
-------
* Bring-up breadcrumbs (P5x / bes_pin) are gone.  EAPOL M1/M3 and most
  per-assoc chatter is bes_devel (needs CONFIG_BES2600_ENABLE_DEVEL_LOGS).
* Keep at info: firmware version/CRC, generated MAC, phy register,
  assoc_mode once per join, 0x0010 send, FAST_PS ok / PS-bad, associated
  scan request/complete/-EBUSY, 0x0008 abort, unjoin complete,
  RETRY_EXCEEDED (ratelimited).
* Factory cali dumps (tx_power_ch_*) are still unprefixed printk.
* wsm_scan_complete_indication still ratelimits "N callbacks suppressed"
  on 14+27 channel scans.

Suspend / resume / shutdown
---------------------------
* Deep suspend removes the STA vif.  On resume, MCU wake fails for tens
  of seconds: bes2600_sdio_active failed / pwr_device_exit_lp_mode,
  active mcu fail, then LMAC station-ID and add_interface recover.
  Screen blank / console dead until power-button is this path, not DRM.
  Fix bes_pwr / SDIO resume so mmc2 comes back without that retry storm.
* Poweroff after a dead SDIO (TX -16) hung NM/wpa 1–3 min: scan.lock
  busy-loop in bes2600_stop, deactive WARN_ON, sdio_tx_work re-queueing
  -EBUSY forever.  Stop must abort the scan with a timeout, mark the bus
  stale after a short -EBUSY streak, and not WARN on deactive failure.
  (deactive no longer WARN_ONs; confirm stop/stale still hold.)

Scan leftovers
--------------
* Drain once at start (do not drop the host count).  After a scan
  timeout, in_progress is 0 while AMPDU may still sit in firmware — the
  LMAC 3s monitor must not mark_bus_stale for leftover bufs (that refused
  0x0006 and skipped every later scan).
* Drain can still leave bufs=20–46 after 500 ms when AMPDU is retrying
  (manual scan while ping/browser).  Starting 0x0007 with a full window
  can still -110 — later item, not a dead bus.
* AMPDU RETRY_EXCEEDED still shows on some 5 GHz BSSIDs after a working
  session.  Leave for now.

Association / rates / aggregation
---------------------------------
* 2.4 GHz is the reliable band here.  Some 5 GHz BSSIDs associate and
  even pass FAST_PS, then drip RETRY_EXCEEDED.  Do not treat 5 GHz auth
  success as "5 GHz is solid".
* EAPOL must not set data_acked or enable BA.  Stay on 1/6 Mbps until a
  non-EAPOL unicast data ACK, then BA (open and WPA2).
* Occasional first 4-way timeout on WPA2: M1 RX, then P53 drop st=9
  (WSM_STATUS_NO_KEY_FOUND) — M3 encrypted before set_key installed the
  PTK.  NM retry / "connect" again works.  Firmware already dropped the
  frame; host cannot decrypt it.  Not an easy driver fix without LMAC
  buffering.
* Do not clamp ICMP/DNS/DHCP to 1 Mbps the way 0d7099 did until that
  change is re-proven on a FAST_PS-ok open BSS.
* Firmware owns BlockAck.  Host ADDBA-Resp is dropped.  Do not
  auto-enable BA after HT ACKs ("connected" with 0% ping).
* Join with leftover hw_bufs_used: often 1 and expected (auth already
  in flight, or a scan/WSM slot after unjoin reset).  prepare_for_join
  host-clears it; late confirms clamp underflow.  Do not poke RX.  Do
  not queue_clear on unjoin.
* wsm_reset drops the firmware TX rate-policy table.  Host cache must
  clear uploaded so MCS policies are sent again on the next BSS.

MAC / interfaces
----------------
* Stable MAC is derived from the SoC serial (locally administered).
  Early dummy vs serial mismatch is still confusing in dmesg; pick one
  story.
* P2P_DEVICE (nl80211 type 10) is host-only.  Do not send WSM on the
  STA if_id for it.  DanctNIX 6.15 disabled P2P_DEVICE; keep or drop
  explicitly.

Bluetooth
---------
* Never worked.  CONFIG_BES2600_BT is off.
* Makefile still lists bes2600_btusb.o; that file is not in the tree.
* /dev/bes2600 (bes_chardev) is leftover vendor userspace control.
  UART hciattach on ttyS1 is the distro workaround.

Hardware / firmware limits (not "just code")
--------------------------------------------
* PineTab2 does not wire BES2600 reset/power GPIOs the way the vendor
  EVB does.  A wedged chip needs a board power cycle.
* Firmware is proprietary (bes2600/best2002_fw_boot_sdio.bin +
  best2002_fw_sdio.bin, Dec 2023).  Fail cleanly if blobs are missing.
  linux-firmware packaging + license is a parallel track for any
  upstream submission.
* Factory calibration comes from bes2600_factory.txt.
* IEEE PS behaviour of this LMAC, and of some APs' FAST_PS, is not
  something the host can fix without documentation or a new blob.

Mainline / staging hygiene (next series, not protocol work)
----------------------------------------------------------
STA on this board is far enough along that more FAST_PS/scan tweaks will
not get the driver into staging.  A reviewable tree needs:

* Rewrite this file as items close (you are here).
* P5x / bes_pin breadcrumbs and most bring-up bes_info are done.
* ITP, nl80211 testmode, and GET_MAC_ADDR_METHOD are gone.
* start_dhcpd() / call_usermodehelper: drop during P2P work, not now.
* /dev/bes2600 (bes_chardev): side project; internal flags still used.
* Makefile still lists bes2600_btusb.o; leave until BT work.  That file
  is not in cw1200 either.
* Makefile -Werror, unused platform variants, Android default paths
  (/data/applog/, /data/cfg/).
* checkpatch.pl --strict on the driver.
* Then an RFC against linux-next staging, with firmware blobs called
  out.  Do not ask to leave staging.  Reviewers will ask whether this
  should be a cw1200 quirk (drivers/net/wireless/st/cw1200) rather than
  a new driver; that merge is later, not the RFC.

Kconfig / build
---------------
* Makefile is Kbuild-only (KERN_DIR / all: modules dropped).  Still has
  ccflags -Werror and hardcoded -DCHIP_WIFI_ROM_VER.
* Drop unused platform variants if PineTab2 is the only in-tree user,
  or isolate them.
* Android-style default paths (/data/applog/, /data/cfg/) do not belong
  in a generic driver.

Dead / leftover code
--------------------
* TODO:COMBO, HACK!!!, commented dump_stack(), #if 0.
* EPTA 0x0029 was a lockup source on a sick bus; do not pile it on
  join/unjoin without a proven need.  BT is unused.
* SDIO TX bounce (tx_pad): do not DMA padded length from the skb.

Lockups already hit (do not reintroduce)
----------------------------------------
* force_close on SDIO CTRL/CMD53 -EBUSY (hard lock CPU / kworker).
* Nested 0x0006 operational-mode while MCU wake failed.
* Scan WARN-loop of 0x0006 / 0x0007 / 0x0029 after a sick bus.
* Host-only unjoin after failed auth skipped wsm_reset; LMAC stayed
  joined; next 0x0007 returned status 13.

Not this driver
---------------
* rockchip-drm swiotlb buffer full.
* QSampleCache wireless-extensions warning.
* systemd-journald "Time jumped backwards".
* typec-extcon / husb311 (board patches, separate).
* Plasma/GNOME screen-blank policy; suspend itself is the driver
  (see Suspend / resume above).

